# Marks, not pack icons

Do not import from `lucide-react`, Heroicons, Phosphor, Radix Icons, Font Awesome, or similar packs. Those glyphs show up on every generated site.

Draw or reuse filled stamps from `src/components/marks.tsx`. Same language as the stall plate: cut corners, crate slats, chalk tallies, punched tickets, street blocks. `currentColor`, `viewBox="0 0 24 24"`. No 24px rounded stroke-2 clones of Lucide.

If a new meaning appears, add a mark there. Chevrons, close, and checks also come from that file. If a shadcn add reintroduces `lucide-react`, replace those icons with marks and drop the import.

```tsx
// BAD
import { Store, Award, Search } from "lucide-react";
<HomePanel icon={Store} />

// GOOD
import { CrateMark, TallyMark, SlatsMark } from "@/components/marks";
<HomePanel icon={CrateMark} />
```
